{
  "profile": "sutra-acquisition-development-cases/v1",
  "qualification": "30 developer-authored synthetic cases. Not independent expert labels, measured costs, probabilities, actual privacy exposure, or real decision authority. Frozen before evaluator. Every model uses two identical candidate proposals only to satisfy the semantic profile; they are not independent evidence.",
  "rules": {
    "worlds": "single: x in {2,4}, true iff x>3; conjunction: x,y in {2,4}, true iff x*y>9.",
    "loss": "choose_true and choose_false cost 10 when incorrect, 0 when correct; abstain always 6. Minimize maximum branch loss plus upper-bound source acquisition and read cost. Source paid once per path; exposure is additive per path. Stop wins ties, otherwise lexical action ID.",
    "labels": "exact: low/high; failed: low+failed/high+failed; overlap: low+mid/high+mid; same: common/common.",
    "sources": "sx for x; shared conjunction uses sx for y, otherwise sy. Costs listed in sx,sy order.",
    "expected": "Manual labels: single exact costs acquisition if not prepaid plus read; conjunction worst branch requires both exact reads, pays distinct nonprepaid sources once; if ambiguous possible outcome or insufficient exposure, some branch remains mixed so no strict benefit vs abstain. Lexical read_x wins symmetric worst-objective ties."
  },
